---
const config=JSON.stringify({servers:{github:{type:'http',url:'https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/'}}},null,2);
const source='https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/blob/main/README.md';
---
<div class="guide"><p><strong>Maintainer-documented — not runtime tested by FreeMCP.</strong> The current GitHub-maintained MCP server supports a hosted HTTP endpoint, including VS Code 1.101+ with OAuth support.</p><p>For VS Code user or workspace <code>mcp.json</code>, the maintainer documents:</p><pre><code>{config}</code></pre><p>Sign in using the client's supported OAuth flow. For clients requiring personal access tokens, use the maintainer's authentication instructions and request only the necessary permissions. Never paste tokens into FreeMCP or commit them to a repository.</p><p><strong>Security:</strong> Depending on granted permissions, GitHub tools may modify repositories, issues, pull requests, and workflows. Review tool approvals and use least-privilege access.</p><p><strong>Source correction:</strong> The current maintained implementation is <a href="https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github/github-mcp-server</a>; the directory's legacy archived listing should be updated after review.</p><a href={source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Maintainer installation and authentication guide ↗</a></div>
<style>.guide{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:20px}.guide p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted)}.guide strong{color:var(--text)}pre{padding:16px;background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;overflow:auto;font-size:12px}.guide a{color:var(--accent)}</style>